.TH PLUGIN-DB 1 "" "plugin-db" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
plugin-db \- pin, show and verify the entries of the plugin database
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B plugin-db
[\fB\-\-store\fR \fIdir\fR | \fB\-\-system\fR] \fBpin\fR \fIaddress\fR [\fB\-\-lv2\-path\fR \fIpath\fR | \fB\-\-file\fR \fIfile.clap\fR] [\fB\-\-layout\fR \fIscheme\fR:\fIsha256\fR]
.br
.B plugin-db
[\fB\-\-store\fR \fIdir\fR | \fB\-\-system\fR] \fBput\fR \fIaddress\fR \fIlayer\fR [\fB\-\-writer\fR \fIname\fR] < body.json
.br
.B plugin-db
[\fB\-\-store\fR \fIdir\fR | \fB\-\-system\fR] \fBshow\fR \fIaddress\fR [\fIhere\fR] [\fB\-\-layout\fR \fIscheme\fR:\fIsha256\fR]
.br
.B plugin-db
[\fB\-\-store\fR \fIdir\fR | \fB\-\-system\fR] \fBquery \-\-json\fR \fIaddress\fR [\fIhere\fR] [\fB\-\-layout\fR \fIscheme\fR:\fIsha256\fR]
.br
.B plugin-db
[\fB\-\-store\fR \fIdir\fR | \fB\-\-system\fR] \fBverify\fR [\fB\-v\fR] [\fIhere\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B plugin-db
keeps one entry for each plugin in a store of layer files. It loads no plugin: it reads LV2 manifests as text and hashes files.
.PP
An address is \fIformat\fR:\fIid\fR, or \fBclap@\fR\fIsha256\fR:\fIid\fR when several files share one CLAP id. The format is
\fBclap\fR or \fBlv2\fR.
.TP
.B pin
Records the plugin's files and parameter layout in the entry. A CLAP plugin is given with \fB\-\-file\fR; an LV2 plugin is
found in \fB\-\-lv2\-path\fR, else LV2_PATH, else ~/.lv2:/usr/local/lib/lv2:/usr/lib/lv2.
.TP
.B put
Writes the layer read from standard input, checked against the store's schema.
.TP
.B show
Prints the attributes, the change and its action, the state, how the plugin runs, the reason, the source, the verdict and
what it was measured under.
.TP
.B query \-\-json
Prints the same answer as one JSON object for scripts and the Zynthian side: the files, layout and record attributes,
the change and its action (or null), the state, how the plugin runs, the reason and the source, the record's tier (the
record's verdict when it says where the plugin runs, else null) and the figures at the rate and quantum given: the
latency measured there, the latency line the record declares, and where one stands against the other (within, over or
unmeasured). A record without the line, or a cell without the figure, is unmeasured. Nothing is computed beyond the
reader's answer; the TypeScript twin and the Python module plugin_db give the same.
.TP
.B verify
Checks every entry as rpm \-V does: one line for each entry that is not current, and exit status 1 when there is one.
\fB\-v\fR prints every entry.
.PP
\fIhere\fR is \fB\-\-machine\-class\fR, \fB\-\-host\fR, \fB\-\-host\-version\fR, \fB\-\-hosting\-epoch\fR, \fB\-\-rules\fR,
\fB\-\-record\-schema\fR, \fB\-\-rate\fR, \fB\-\-quantum\fR and \fB\-\-fact\fR \fIkey\fR=\fIvalue\fR. A fact not given is not
known, and no record matches it.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I $PLUGIN_DB_STORE
The store. Otherwise /var/lib/plugin-db with \fB\-\-system\fR, else $XDG_STATE_HOME/plugin-db (~/.local/state/plugin-db).
.TP
.I /usr/share/plugin-db/store.schema.json
The JSON Schema of a layer file.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 on success, 1 when \fBverify\fR finds an entry that is not current or a command fails, 2 on a usage error.
.SH LICENSE
GPL-3.0-or-later.
